  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solar Mills: from R&amp;D to commercialisation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project has: 1) produced the world&#x2019;s most efficient, smart and affordable small milling machine ever developed, and 2) seen a proof-of-concept roll-out that overwhelmingly demonstrates strong customer demand and high levels of customer satisfaction. 

This is the first time a viable solar milling solution has been commercially sold at any relative scale in the market. Until now diesel mills have been the only mechanised option for small holder farmers, but the results of this project herald a new era for off-grid milling and the days of the diesel mill are numbered. 

The Agsol MicroMill v2 designed under this project is a revolutionary product that is poised to change how half a billion people in rural Sub-Saharan Africa process their essential staple foods. The MicroMill is not an incremental improvement on current technology, it represents a complete step change.

The core features of the MicroMill that were developed under this project and make it so special are three entirely custom or industry first innovations. These include:
1)Custom designed and build brushless DC (BLDC) motor. The case for direct drive and super efficient milling is so unique there is not a suitable motor on the market. It has to be DC (for solar), water/dust proof, very high speed for efficient milling, and accommodate very high vibration.
2)Custom designed BLDC motor driver, power electronics, and governing firmware that ensures the machine is operating at peak performance and always protected.
3)Industry first passive and closed loop feed regulating mechanism that maintains consistent power consumption across a wide range of milled products. From the user perspective, it means they can dump the grains in and the mill will automatically take care of everything else.</narrative>
  </description>
